5️⃣ Now the time required to load the extra components is delayed to the moment when the user
    navigates to /races, /register or /login. 🔥🔥But we can ask Angular to preload these chunks when
    the application is done loading and idle. With this option, our users won’t even have to wait for
    the chunk to be downloaded when they click on a link. To do so, add
    withPreloading(PreloadAllModules) as an additional parameter to the
    provideRouter(routes, withComponentInputBinding()) call in app.config.ts. Now if you reload your
    app, you’ll see that the chunks are downloaded just after the end of the page load.
    app.config.ts:

        export const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {
            providers: [
                // omitted
                provideRouter(routes, withComponentInputBinding(), 👉 withPreloading(PreloadAllModules))
            ]
        };
    


